.th IMPORT I 8/12/77
.sh NAME
import - copy a file from an Interdata OS/MT disc
.sh SYNOPSIS
import device file [ outfile ]
.sh DESCRIPTION
Reads the specified file from the device,
which must contain an Interdata OS file system,
and copies it onto
.it outfile
(if given)
or to the standard output.

.it import
translates the filename to uppercase before searching
the OS directory.
.sh AUTHOR
R Miller
.br
University of Wollongong
.sh "SEE ALSO"
dfi(I), export(I)
.sh BUGS
Can only read INDEXED and CONTIGUOUS files.
.br
Doesn't know about "Dynamic OS/MT" directory format.
